IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il40-nouns`
IMPORT `il40-seat`

-- TESTS of the seat layer: each exported question, asked with plain inputs, answers as the text says.  Hand-derived from the text of ss 4, 6(a), 8, 9, 10 and 11.

§ `Tests: the seat`

#ASSERT `What status does the Basic Law give to my language` Hebrew EQUALS JUST `the language of the State`
#ASSERT `What status does the Basic Law give to my language` Arabic EQUALS JUST `a special status in the State`
#ASSERT `What status does the Basic Law give to my language` English EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the rule on my use of Arabic in an instrument that s 4(b) counts as law` `a law of the Knesset`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the rule on my use of Arabic in an instrument that s 4(b) counts as law` `a regulation`)
#ASSERT `Does s 4(c) leave my status of Arabic unharmed` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) `only a status given in practice` `the commencement day is declined` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does s 4(c) leave my status of Arabic unharmed` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) `only a status given in practice` `the commencement day is declined` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does s 4(c) leave my status of Arabic unharmed` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) `a status given in practice and a status an enactment gave` `the commencement day is declined` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does s 6(a) put on the State a duty to endeavour to secure my safety` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this calendar an official calendar of the State` `the Gregorian calendar` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `What standing does s 9 give to this day` `Independence Day` EQUALS JUST `the official national holiday of the State`
#ASSERT `Is this one of the fixed days of rest of the State` `the Sabbath` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I have the right to keep the days of rest on my own Sabbath and festivals` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was a change to the Basic Law made as s 11 requires` `a Basic Law` 61 120
#ASSERT NOT (`Was a change to the Basic Law made as s 11 requires` `a law of the Knesset` 120 120)
